Disagreements: D group (colleagues 1,3,4) claims D remains obligated post-2022 drop because 30 employees on Jan 1 2022; C group (2,5,6,9) claims only C violates via monthly updates + quarterly distribution (exceeds 30-day window) while others are below threshold or compliant. A/B outliers focus on timing/distribution edge cases. 

Evidence favors C: threshold is Jan-1 snapshot each year, so D (24 employees Jan 1 2023) has no 2023 obligation; C's explicit quarterly distribution after monthly revisions clearly breaches timing rule. Preserve: distribution timing details, headcount snapshot rule, and that only C is above threshold yet non-compliant.}

