PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts (ESA Ontario): 25+ employees on Jan 1 of relevant year triggers written disconnect-from-work policy (due ~Mar 2022) + electronic-monitoring policy (due Oct 2022); each must be distributed to all staff (incl. new hires) within 30 days of prep/revision/hire. Status re-assessed yearly on Jan 1; threshold met in prior year creates obligation even if headcount later drops (disputed). 

Round 1 split: D (colleagues 1,4) persists after drop below 25 on 1 Jan 2023; C (2,3,5,6,8,9) violates 30-day rule via monthly updates + quarterly distribution; B (7,10) distribution duty applies even to voluntary policies below threshold. A ignored.

Unresolved: exact persistence after headcount drop; whether “appropriately distributed” satisfies quarterly cadence; if voluntary policies trigger statutory distribution. My prior view leans C (annual reassessment extinguishes D; 30-day breach clear in C) but need to confirm 2023 counting date controls ongoing duty.}

