7.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B remains the clearest ongoing breach. The employer in B already prepared both required policies well before the statutory deadlines and has maintained them continuously, so the only live issue is the distribution obligation. The ESA still mandates that copies reach every employee—including new hires—within 30 days of hire or any revision; an explicit, cost-based refusal to provide those copies is a direct and continuing violation that exists on 2 January 2023 regardless of the 23-employee headcount.  

By contrast, the employer in C meets the threshold, maintains both policies, and distributes them on a recurring quarterly schedule after each monthly update. The statute’s language is “as soon as practicable,” not a rigid 30-day clock; ordinary business-cycle timing for routine revisions can reasonably satisfy that standard, and nothing in the text requires literal hand-delivery within 30 days when the policies remain live and accessible.  

Options A, D and E never crossed the 25-employee threshold on the relevant January 1 dates, so neither policy is mandatory for them. This leaves B’s deliberate non-distribution as the only active contravention visible on the date in question.}

